course: dictionary
lesson: 12905
title: Err: making mistakes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Err is a formal word. It means to make a mistake or to be wrong. «Everyone can err, so do not be upset when you get a sum wrong.» The sentence tells you that mistakes are normal, so err must mean make a mistake.
explain: Err appears in a famous saying: «To err is human.» The clue is the word human. People make mistakes, and that is natural. The saying does not mean mistakes are good, only that everyone makes them sometimes.
explain: The phrase «err on the side of caution» is useful when you are not sure. It means you choose the safer of two options. «The ice looked thin, so we erred on the side of caution and stayed on the path.» Staying on the path was the safer choice.
fact: Err is a verb: err, errs, erred, erring.
fact: «Err» means to make a mistake or to be wrong.
fact: «To err is human» means that making mistakes is a natural part of being a person.
fact: «Err on the side of caution» means to choose the safer of two choices.
fact: Err is a formal word, and in old church language it can mean to do wrong or to sin.
exercise: «I think I may have erred in my sum, so I will check it again.» What does erred mean here? | Finished early | Won a prize | Went for a long walk | *Made a mistake
exercise: Mum says, «When you are not sure, err on the side of caution.» What should you do? | *Choose the safer option | Shout for help | Choose the riskiest option | Ignore the problem
exercise: Which saying means that making mistakes is natural for people? | Wet through and cold | Hold your breath | *To err is human | Out of time, out of luck
test: «Even the best scientists sometimes err.» What does err mean in this sentence? | Sing loudly | Fall asleep | *Be wrong | Win a race
test: Which choice fits the phrase «err on the side of caution» when the ice looks thin? | Skip the warning sign | Run across the lake | Jump off the high wall | *Wait for a grown-up to check the ice first
exam: In «To err is human, to forgive divine», what does err mean? | To run very quickly | To be very tall | *To make a mistake | To sing a song
